Stabwound wrote:
> I consider myself a fairly good Nethack player, but I find that I take far 
> too long (in terms of turns spent) in each ascension.

Personally I don't think there is a right amount of time; my longest 
game was just over 50,000 turns and my archeologist got killed on 
Astral. Most of my ascensions have been in the 30-40k turn range. 
However, I have read awesome ascensions of 
polyless/genoless/wishless/pacifist etc healers who take 300k turns or more.

The only concern I ever have with ascension time is when I play wizards, 
because their spells have to be relearned every 20k turns, and books are 
only good for 1 relearn or so unless rewritten.


  > I believe that my main problem is overpreparing for Gehennom. I 
don't think
> I've ever stepped foot past the VoTD without at least -30AC. I'm starting to 
> think that is overkill. What would be a safe minimum AC to tackle Gehennom 
> and beyond?

There is no such thing as "safe minimum AC." You are in danger 
constantly until you get a DYWYPI at your diety's high altar after 
saccing the true Amulet of Yendor. Especially in Gehennom. There is also 
no such thing as too many ways to remove a curse on an ascension run, 
and there is no such thing as too many HP. Trust me, you'll be glad you 
beefed up the first time you have Yeenogho on the left and Demogorgon on 
the right, with some master liches and minotaurs thrown in for fun.

Is that paranoid? You bet. But paranoia is a nethacker's best friend.

> 
> Also, how do people generally handle stashes?

I bless my BoH and get my strength up as far as I can. I don't 
personally stash. You never know when you'll need that stuff. That is 
just a matter of taste, however. If stashes keep you alive, then stash.
